            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0294" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12099: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-08-09T19:00:00+08:00">August 9, 1932—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 9—8:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>924. Following from American Consul General at Nanking: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“August 8, noon. I learn from apparently reliable sources that Lo Wen-kan
                            is still attending his office as concurrent Minister for Foreign Affairs
                            and that Huang Shao-hsiung, Minister of the Interior, will return from
                            Shanghai tonight and will be in temporary charge of the office of the
                            President of the Executive Yuan.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
